# Climate, fan and water-heater controls

Show what the room is doing and what the equipment has been asked to do. A measured temperature, a target, a selected mode and the reported activity are different facts. Do not merge them into one dial.

These examples are simulated with invented data. They do not control any equipment. This page covers the design contract (HA-CTRL-005, from gap HA-GAP-005). It does not add a thermostat, fan service or hot-water automation.

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-capabilities">Task and capability contract</h2>

| Domain | Keep apart, and offer only what the entity supports |
| --- | --- |
| Climate | `current_temperature` and the target; the selected HVAC mode and the reported `hvac_action`; a single target and, where supported, lower and upper targets. |
| Fan | On or off, percentage, preset, oscillation and direction are separate capabilities. Keep a preset’s supplied name. |
| Humidifier or dehumidifier | Measured humidity and target humidity. The device class says whether it adds or removes moisture, so do not reverse that to suit an icon. |
| Water heater | The reported operation mode, the target where available, and the current measurement. Keep the equipment’s own instructions and protections. |
| Every numeric target | The native unit, limits, increment and precision. Check a lower and upper pair before sending a request. |

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-states">States, pending work and failure</h2>

Selected Heat with reported Idle is valid. It does not mean a fault or that the system is heating. Off is not unavailable. When the measurement is missing, keep a known target visible with its own label. When the target is not known, never show the measured temperature in its place.

Keep a requested target as a draft or pending value until the documented confirmation arrives. If the mode changes during an edit, do not send a target to a mode that no longer supports it, and keep the draft for review where the application does so. For a rejected target, show the range error at the field. For a failed request, show the failure for the task. Do not diagnose a boiler, refrigerant or air-quality fault from an unconfirmed request.

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-content">Content and interpretation</h2>

Where wording could be ambiguous, use “Measured temperature”, “Target temperature”, “Selected mode” and “Reported activity”. Keep the °C, °F or percentage unit next to each value. A humidity setting is not a medical assessment. Defer to the equipment instructions and competent advice for water-heater settings. This design system does not set a safe temperature or change protective programmes.

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-accessibility">Accessibility and interaction</h2>

Give targets and modes labelled native controls with keyboard adjustment and readable units. Do not require dragging round a circular thermostat to enter a precise value. Announce a target change once, separately from frequent temperature readings. At enlarged text, keep both setpoints readable. Never hide one behind a tooltip or show it by colour alone.

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-005-integration">Native integration boundary</h2>

Use the native Climate, Fan, Humidifier and Water heater controls with the modes and features the entity supports. Keep the entity’s unit conversion and precision. The pinned climate source in the gap inventory is source evidence, not a live check of every device.

